st closed off the row, and Black's stone at D7 did nothing for the trouble below."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "The 20k answered with E7, which lost 13.9 points and brought the game back from -21.5 to -7.6. It was White's worst move, and it let Black back into a game that looked lost."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "After White's H4 swung things to +1.1 for Black, D8 lost 9.3 points and sent it back to -8.2. The engine preferred F8, and Black was still giving back ground it had just won."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "The endgame decided the result. G9 lost 4.4 points, from +4.3 to -0.1, and the engine's choice was H9. From here both sides traded small losses, and Black finished at +2.0 on the last pass."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every command only parsed board text (the `inspect` function listing chains and liberties, or applying one manually named candidate move and removing captured chains), counted empty regions, replayed the actual game record, or wrote notes and SGF files. Nothing looped over candidate moves, scored or ranked them, or played any sequence forward, so no move search occurred.", "stop": false}}